&lt;p data-start=&quot;162&quot; data-end=&quot;733&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Team &amp;amp; About Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik&#39;s sales organisation is a unified group of elite cross-functional professionals helping companies across every major industry achieve true resilience against cyberattacks, malicious insiders, and operational disruptions. As Named Account Executive in Germany, you&#39;ll own a portfolio of large enterprise accounts, driving Rubrik&#39;s continued expansion in one of Europe&#39;s most dynamic enterprise markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and grow a portfolio of enterprise accounts across Germany, combining existing customer relationships with new business development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run full, multistakeholder sales cycles end to end — from discovery and qualification through solution design, negotiation, and close — across both net-new logo and existing-account expansion deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a high-quality pipeline across your territory, balancing larger strategic opportunities with faster-moving transactional deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop executive relationships within your accounts, translating Rubrik&#39;s technical capabilities into the board-level priorities that make data security a strategic imperative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Solutions Engineers, Channel Development, and Rubrik&#39;s partner ecosystem to extend reach across your territory and position Rubrik against the full scope of customer risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with and learn from your regional peers — the German team works closely together on deal strategy and account coverage, so you&#39;ll grow fastest by leaning on each other.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed market intelligence back to Rubrik&#39;s leadership, including competitive signals and account trends that shape our go-to-market approach across Germany.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience You&#39;ll Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience closing complex enterprise deals, with the appetite to grow into larger, multi-product opportunities — we&#39;ll help you build the rest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record that shows both new-logo acquisition and growing existing customer relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in German and professional in English; you engage confidently with both technical buyers and executive stakeholders in either language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of enterprise buying cycles, procurement processes, and multistakeholder decision-making within large or complex organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with channel partners and distributors as part of a broader go-to-market motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel regularly across your territory to build in-person relationships with customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in cybersecurity, data protection, backup/recovery, or adjacent infrastructure/cloud categories — candidates who understand the difference between data centre and cloud environments tend to ramp fastest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with MEDDPICC as a sales qualification and execution framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships within large German enterprise or Mittelstand organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Salesforce for pipeline management and forecast accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
